  "body": "## What changed\nThe program sim's column engine, which feeds the post gate's verdict, now sweeps XY arcs (G2/G3 in G17) on the **true circle**. Before, it cut them as chords drawn inside the arc.\n\n**Why:** the inside chords err on both sides.\n- **False gouge (#402):** near a convex corner, the arc's centre is the part's corner, so the chords bring the simulated tool up to one sagitta closer to the part than the real arc. On the issue's L-block, one 0.375 mm column 0.088 mm inside the riser corner was clipped. Judged by height alone, that read as a 10 mm gouge, and the post gate refused a clean 2D Contour.\n- **Hidden real cuts:** at a concave corner the part lies outside the arc, and the chords stopped up to one sagitta (`cell/4`) short of the wall. A small over-cut there went unseen. On a bull-nose helix arc, a column the true arc cuts 2.5 mm deep was missed.\n\n**Fix:** a new `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/dexel_arc.rs` (302 lines, provenance header) sweeps every tool shape (flat disc, ball, cone, bull nose) along the exact arc.\n- **Reach window:** for each column, the reachable stretch of arc has a closed form from the circle-point distance law (`d² = (R−ρ)² + 4Rρ·sin²(u/2)`).\n- **Flat tools and level arcs:** exact.\n- **Helical ball, cone and bull arcs:** the window is split where the bottom's curvature can change sign, and each piece is searched with samples plus a golden section. The search only returns real evaluations, so it never cuts deeper than the tool went.\n- **Arc end points** are judged as discs.\n- **Unchanged:** XZ/YZ arcs keep their chords, the gouge verdict (`deviate`) gets no slack or tolerance, and #299 / #303 are untouched.\n\n**Why it's conservative both ways:** the simulated swept area *is* the real arc's swept area. It cannot reach toward the part where the real tool didn't, and it cannot leave material the real arc cut. Alternatives considered and dropped (in `docs/decisions/402-arc-chord-sagitta.md`):\n- outside chords, which hide concave gouges;\n- mixed chords, which over-cut both ways;\n- an exact arc only in the verdict, which leaves the stock wrong and is close to #299's slack question;\n- finer chords, which only shrink the error.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- **New `app/tests/contour_arc_sim.rs`:** the issue's MCP job on the L-block. The post gate reports no gouge. This failed before the fix.\n- **New `sim/tests/arc_sweep.rs`** (5 tests; the old code fails 4):\n  - flat-tool exactness, including sweeps over 180° and a sweep crossing ±180°;\n  - every tool shape, level and helical, matched against a dense true-arc scan;\n  - the issue's own lattice, column (146,13);\n  - a **planted convex gouge** (corner arc R 2.5 with a 3 mm tool), still convicted at 10 mm;\n  - a **concave fillet** case: clean when correct, and when over-cut by 0.06 mm, it flags exactly the wall columns the true arc reaches.\n- **Rewritten in place:** `stock_sim::arc_chords_under_sweep_so_the_sim_only_over_reports` is now `xy_arcs_sweep_the_true_arc_whatever_the_chord_budget`, so the test count is unchanged. The old name asserted the chords were conservative, which they weren't.\n- **`stock_bull_nose::both_engines_cut_a_bull_nose_alike`:** straight moves still need 1e-5 agreement. The helix arc now uses `arc_parity`, which allows the field engine's chord error away from the cut's edge, because the field engine still chords. That is filed as **#413**.\n\n## Readings\n- The worker ran the batch tier: geometry, cl, tools, post, sim and app all pass, including `golden_cl`, `posting`, `stock_sim_document`, `setup_carry`, `stock_engine_agreement` and `rotary_field_parity`.\n- No golden changed.\n- clippy `-D warnings` is clean for all crates.\n- **Quick gate after merging upstream/main** (clean): post, sim and app are green. The remaining reds also fail on main: `swarf_pose_continuity` (#351) and the GPU headless tests.\n- **Side effect:** rest material and 3D roughing's prior stock (`machining3d::feed` uses `Dexel::subtract`) now also see the exact arc.\n\n**For the maintainer:** this changes the simulator behind the post gate's verdict. Please give it a close look, even though it is flagged ready.\n\nChangelog: The program sim cuts XY arcs on the true circle instead of inscribed chords, so the post gate no longer reports a false gouge at a convex arc corner and no longer misses a sub-sagitta cut at a concave one (#402)\n\nFixes #402\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
